WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.260
Marvel's bigwigs have a knack for topnotch
casting, and Black Panther, the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.290
Universe's 2018 venture into the Kingdom of
Wakanda, is no exception.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.891
This film's sprawling cast includes familiar
faces and new additions to the MCU, and, as

00:00:13.891 --> 00:00:18.599
you may have already noticed, many of Wakanda's
heroes and villains look — and sound — very

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:19.599
familiar.

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:22.970
Let's take a look at where you've already
seen the talented men and women behind Marvel's

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.420
Black Panther.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.189
Chadwick Boseman - T'Challa/Black Panther

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:31.670
As king of the isolated Kingdom of Wakanda
and the man behind the Black Panther mask,

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.580
T'Challa has become both the political and
literal protector of his people following

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.750
the death of his father, T'Chaka, during the
events of Captain America: Civil War.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.790
So we'd say he probably has a few more responsibilities
than the average guy.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:47.680
T'Challa actor Chadwick Boseman has appeared
in a number of hugely successful bio-pics,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.470
portraying Jackie Robinson in 42, James Brown
in Get On Up, and a young Thurgood Marshall

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.250
in the aptly titled Marshall.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.300
But the British American Drama Academy graduate
got his start with a series of minor roles

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.230
in procedural dramas and soaps in the early
2000s.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:07.560
In 2010, he landed his first recurring role
on the psychological drama Persons Unknown.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.700
Not bad — especially considering Boseman,
who's also a playwright, initially wanted

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.670
to stick to writing and directing.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.210
Danai Gurira - Okoye

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:20.490
Okoye may seem like a newcomer to Marvel fans
who stick to the flicks, but, in the comics,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.939
she plays a pivotal role in the survival of
not only T'Challa himself, but the whole of

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:25.939
Wakanda.

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:30.299
As a member of the reinstated Dora Milaje
— T'Challa's personal order of bodyguards

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:34.819
— Okoye is tasked with protecting Black
Panther at all costs…even if he doesn't

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:36.569
look like he needs much protection.

00:01:36.569 --> 00:01:41.240
It's no surprise that actress Danai Gurira's
Marvel counterpart looks like she knows how

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.200
to handle herself with a deadly weapon.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.350
After all, she trained with a legit sword
master in preparation to play Michonne on

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.070
AMC's The Walking Dead.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.700
She's also shown off the acting chops she
developed at the Tisch School of the Arts,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.649
going on to portray one half of a Nigerian
couple struggling through fertility issues

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.170
in the 2013 drama Mother of George.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:05.130
She'd return to the big screen in the 2017
biopic All Eyez on Me, playing Afeni Shakur,

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.329
mother of late rapper Tupac Shakur.

00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:10.440
Michael B. Jordan - Erik Stevens/Killmonger

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:15.050
When Erik Stevens chose his supervillain pseudonym,
subtlety must have been the last thing on

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.050
his mind.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.409
We all know what kind of message a guy with
the name "Killmonger" is trying to get across.

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:23.840
A former black ops soldier with a vendetta
against T'Challa, Killmonger finds himself

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.680
teaming up with arms dealer Klaue in his quest
for the Wakandan throne.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.120
If you've got any taste in TV, you'll immediately
recognize actor Michael B. Jordan from his

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.650
portrayal of Wallace in The Wire.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.610
Following his season-long stint on the HBO
hit, Jordan took his talents to Friday Night

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.190
Lights, joining the cast for its fourth and
fifth seasons as Vince Howard.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:47.120
In 2013, Jordan worked with future Black Panther
director Ryan Coogler, portraying shooting

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.360
victim Oscar Grant in 2015's Fruitvale Station.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:54.819
He'd later earn acclaim for his work in the
Rocky spinoff Creed — and star in the ill-fated

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:59.140
Fantastic Four reboot, but we don't need to
talk about that here.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.510
Lupita Nyong'o - Nakia

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.829
Like Okoye, Nakia is a member of the Dora
Milaje — but rather than remaining by King

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:10.579
T'Challa's side, the blade-wielding spy sneaks
around the globe, gathering intel to keep

00:03:10.579 --> 00:03:14.010
the isolated nation of Wakanda protected and
informed.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.431
Actress Lupita Nyong'o got her first big break
in the heartrending 12 Years a Slave, which

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.629
snagged the young star an Oscar for Best Supporting
Actress.

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:26.040
But sci-fi and fantasy fans will most likely
recognize her as the voice of Maz Kanata in

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.810
the Star Wars sequel trilogy.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.640
She also provided a vocal performance for
The Jungle Book's Raksha, wolf mother to Mowgli,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.750
in the 2016 live-action reimagining.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.879
Forest Whitaker - Zuri

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:42.489
Drawing comparisons to Star Wars' Obi-Wan
Kenobi, Zuri is a spiritual figure akin to

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:45.819
a shaman with strong links to T'Challa's father,
T'Chaka.

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:50.170
Part of the Black Panther's inner circle,
Zuri plays many roles, including advisor,

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.540
mentor, and spiritual guide to the young Wakandan
King.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.560
Forest Whitaker is an actor renowned for his
adaptability.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.750
In other words: no matter what kind of films
you're into, chances are you've seen this

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.910
brilliant actor somewhere.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.290
Dig a gruesome, gritty historical piece every
now and then?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:09.280
You'll recognize Whitaker from his portrayal
of former Ugandan president Idi Amin in 2008's

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.510
The Last King of Scotland.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:13.359
Into genre-bending hip-hop samurai bloodbaths?

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:14.400
No prob.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.729
You'll know him as the titular character from
Jim Jarmusch's Ghost Dog: The Way of the Samurai.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:23.020
And, as his appearance in Black Panther attests,
he isn't averse to the occasional blockbuster

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.880
— in fact, he was recently seen in a galaxy
far, far away, playing the guerrilla Rebel

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.970
known as Saw Gerrera in Rogue One: A Star
Wars Story.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.130
Angela Bassett - Ramonda

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.660
The recently widowed Queen Mother of Wakanda,
Ramonda has seen better days since the death

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.530
of her late husband and former Wakandan king
T'Chaka.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:45.840
But even in the face of such personal and
political tragedy, Queen Ramonda persists

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.300
as a driving force on her son's high council.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.750
Angela Bassett, who portrays the Wakandan
matriarch in MCU's Black Panther, has cemented

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.030
herself as a veritable legend on the big and
small screens.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:05:00.870
In the '90s, she starred in a string of critically
acclaimed films like Malcolm X, What's Love

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:04.640
Got to Do With It, How Stella Got Her Groove
Back, and Waiting to Exhale.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.590
But Bassett would later bring her talents
to television, nabbing big roles in a number

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:14.490
of Ryan Murphy-run shows like American Horror
Story and FOX police procedural 9-1-1 alongside

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.410
fellow AHS alum Connie Britton.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.580
Daniel Kaluuya - W'Kabi

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:24.590
Hostile toward outsiders and endlessly loyal
to his allies — especially T'Challa — W'Kabi

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.270
is a force to be reckoned with.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:30.520
Not only is W'Kabi Black Panther's right-hand
man, but the chief of Wakandan security is

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.349
also a capable warrior to boot.

00:05:32.349 --> 00:05:37.241
W'Kabi actor Daniel Kaluuya appeared in a
handful of films in the early 2000s — along

00:05:37.241 --> 00:05:41.520
with a recurring role in the British drama
Skins and a well-received performance in an

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.979
episode of Black Mirror.

00:05:42.979 --> 00:05:47.880
But it was a minor role in 2013's Kick-Ass
2 as Black Death that jumpstarted his rise

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.880
to fame.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.020
He would go on to become a household name
in 2017, when he starred in the award-winning

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.650
psychological thriller Get Out.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.820
Florence Kasumba - Ayo

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:03.479
A member of the Dora Milaje, Ayo leads T'Challa's
security unit with confidence and poise.

00:06:03.479 --> 00:06:07.639
Introduced to viewers in Captain America:
Civil War, she nearly came to blows with Black

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:11.560
Widow, during a confrontation about everybody's
favorite big cat on campus.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:15.449
While she's appeared in a number of German
shows and movies, actress Florence Kasumba

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:18.520
is still relatively new to American film and
television.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.080
The soon-to-be star has only appeared in a
handful of productions like 2017's hugely

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.330
successful Wonder Woman movie in which she
played Senator Acantha.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:32.180
And in 2016, she joined the cast of the short-lived
Emerald City, an edgy reimagining of The Wizard

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:35.440
of Oz in which she played the Wicked Witch
of the East.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.360
Letitia Wright - Shuri

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.250
T'Challa's half-sister Shuri is definitely
a runner-up for biggest badass in Wakanda.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:46.449
With super smarts to rival the likes of Tony
Stark and a penchant for powerful weaponry

00:06:46.449 --> 00:06:50.650
— like her panther-faced blaster gloves
— Shuri isn't afraid to take her tech-savvy

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:54.629
talents to the battlefield alongside her brother
and the Dora Milaje.

00:06:54.629 --> 00:06:58.159
Let's get one thing straight: Letitia Wright
deserves all the roles.

00:06:58.159 --> 00:07:02.491
She showed that she could lead a feature film
in 2015, when she took center stage in the

00:07:02.491 --> 00:07:04.289
award-winning Urban Hymn.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:09.629
In fact, 2015 proved a huge year for Wright:
not only did she snag a recurring role in

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:14.099
the sci-fi drama Humans, but she was also
tapped to portray a central character in the

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:16.379
Doctor Who episode "Face the Raven."

00:07:16.379 --> 00:07:20.539
While she's mostly credited with bit roles
in British television shows like Top Boy,

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:25.270
Coming Up, and Chasing Shadows, she also starred
in the Black Mirror episode "Black Museum"

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:29.240
as Nish, a visitor to the titular tourist
attraction.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.530
Winston Duke - M'Baku

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:36.280
M'Baku — known in the Black Panther comics
as the super offensively named Man-Ape — will

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:41.180
thankfully not be taking his source material's
pseudonym when he makes his MCU debut.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:45.639
However, the young Jabari tribe leader doesn't
look any less menacing, even if he's swapped

00:07:45.639 --> 00:07:49.550
out his comic counterpart's full gorilla hide
suit for more practical armor.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:54.470
While M'Baku is a pretty well-known and feared
comic book villain, the man behind the tattered

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.509
breastplate, Winston Duke, is relatively new
to acting.

00:07:57.509 --> 00:08:02.481
Duke, who has a background in theatre, began
his television acting career in 2014 when

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:06.349
he guest starred on an episode of Law and
Order: Special Victims Unit as a high school

00:08:06.349 --> 00:08:07.430
football player.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:11.380
That same year, the actor returned to the
crime thriller genre, portraying Mini in a

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.949
seven-episode arc of CBS crime thriller Person
of Interest.

00:08:15.949 --> 00:08:18.479
Martin Freeman - Everett Ross

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:23.099
First introduced in Captain America: Civil
War, Everett Ross is a CIA operative and former

00:08:23.099 --> 00:08:25.570
head of the Joint Terrorism Task Force.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.360
In Black Panther, Ross finds himself at odds
with the vibranium-hungry Ulysses Klaue.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.320
As it turns out, the smuggler isn't exactly
about to go down without a fight.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:39.580
Actor Martin Freeman is everywhere: from portraying
Dr. John H. Watson in BBC's Sherlock opposite

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.660
fellow MCU-er Benedict Cumberbatch to stepping
into the furry, oversized feet of Bilbo Baggins

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:49.700
in the Hobbit trilogy, Freeman's filmography
resembles a laundry list of big-name flicks,

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.490
quirky TV shows, and everything in between.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:56.250
After getting his big break on the British
version of The Office, Freeman would go on

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.779
to star in a number of mostly comedic films
including Edgar Wright's Three Flavours Cornetto

00:09:00.779 --> 00:09:06.110
Trilogy and 2005's The Hitchhiker's Guide
to the Galaxy, in which he played reluctant

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.010
and newly-evicted-from-Earth protagonist Arthur
Dent.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.570
Andy Serkis - Ulysses Klaue

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.450
One of the most exciting new additions to
the Marvel Cinematic Universe has got to be

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:21.430
Ulysses Klaue, our resident sociopathic South
African arms dealer who was first introduced

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.329
in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:28.760
While actor Andy Serkis brings sadistic charm
and a roguish look to the role, comic fans

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:34.320
will likely associate the name "Klaw" with
Marvel's token sonic disruptor-wielding supervillain

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.450
made of living sound.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:40.630
Believe it or not, mo-cap mogul Andy Serkis
had only been working on TV and film for around

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:45.580
six years before Peter Jackson cast him as
Gollum in The Fellowship of the Ring in 2001.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:50.690
It was this role that inspired the "cyber-thespian"
to dedicate his career — or, at least, a

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.410
good chunk of it — to motion capture performance.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:58.410
Serkis reprised his role as Gollum in Jackson's
The Hobbit trilogy, and he's lent his talent

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:01.220
to the Star Wars sequel films as Supreme Leader
Snoke.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:06.450
But he's perhaps best known for his portrayal
of Caesar, the tragic protagonist of the Planet

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.120
of the Apes films.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.180
Thanks for watching!

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.769
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:11.769 --> 00:10:13.370
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

